        "stepByStepSolution": "Step 1: Calculate gravimetric mass percentages:\nTotal sample mass = 500 kg.\n(1) Biodegradable fraction: (210 kg / 500 kg) × 100% = 42.0%.\n(2) Non-biodegradable synthetic plastic fraction: ((135 kg + 65 kg) / 500 kg) × 100% = (200 kg / 500 kg) × 100% = 40.0%.\nStep 2: Fluid dynamic mechanism of storm culvert occlusion:\nBuoyant LDPE water sachets and PET bottles float on stormwater runoff and aggregate at culvert inlets and bridge grates, forming an impermeable physical 'plastic dam'.\nSilt and sand deposit against this barrier, reducing channel cross-sectional area (A) and drastically increasing Manning's hydraulic roughness coefficient (n).\nAccording to Manning's flow equation (Q = (1/n) × A × R^(2/3) × S^(1/2)), discharge capacity Q plummets far below storm inflow, causing hydraulic backwater to overtop embankments and submerge residential areas.\nStep 3: Propose interventions:\nImmediate engineering: (1) Install automated mechanical trash rakes and upstream heavy-duty steel deflection boom screens; (2) Excavate silt-trap retention basins upstream.\nLong-term policy: (1) Mandatory source segregation in school canteens and homes using color-coded bins linked to plastic buy-back centers; (2) Enforce municipal sanitation bye-laws with spot fines for littering and enforce extended producer responsibility (EPR) on plastic manufacturers.",
