        "stepByStepSolution": "Step 1: Chemical reaction equations:\nAerobic Respiration: C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ → 6CO₂ + 6H₂O + Heat.\nAnaerobic Methanogenic Fermentation: C₆H₁₂O₆ → 3CH₄ + 3CO₂.\nStep 2: Calculate weekly methane mass generation:\nMolar mass of C₆H₁₂O₆ = 180 g/mol; 3 moles of CH₄ = 48 g.\nTheoretical maximum yield = 48 / 180 = 0.2667 kg CH₄ per kg biomass.\nWith 40% anaerobic conversion efficiency: Mass of CH₄ = 10,000 kg × 0.2667 × 0.40 = 1,066.8 kg CH₄/week.\nStep 3: Calculate Equivalent Carbon Dioxide Footprint (CO₂-eq):\nCO₂-eq = Mass of CH₄ × GWP = 1,066.8 kg × 28 = 29,870.4 kg CO₂-eq (≈ 29.87 metric tonnes CO₂-eq per week).\nStep 4: Benefits of Aerobic Composting:\n1. Climate Mitigation: Aerobic bacteria inhibit obligate anaerobic methanogens, emitting only short-cycle biogenic CO₂ (GWP = 1) instead of high-potency methane (GWP = 28), eliminating ~30 tonnes CO₂-eq weekly.\n2. Agricultural Enrichment: Generates stable, nutrient-dense humus bio-fertilizer rich in nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium, improving soil water retention and cutting synthetic fertilizer costs.",
